---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
import CloudOrSelfHosted from '../../components/partials/CloudOrSelfHosted.astro'
import FAQSection from '../../components/FAQSection.astro'
import {vikunjaCloudSignupLink} from '../../helpers/vikunjaCloudLink'

const faqs = [
    {
        question: 'Can I import my Planka boards into Vikunja?',
        answer: 'Yes. Planka has no native export ([open issue](https://github.com/plankanban/planka/issues/670)), only a REST API, so Vikunja\'s [Planka importer](/help/import-and-export/#importing-from-planka) talks to that API directly. You enter your Planka URL and an API key (or username and password), and it brings over projects, boards, lists, cards, labels, due dates, comments, attachments, and cover images. Checklists and custom fields land in the task description. Credentials are used for the import only and not stored.',
    },
    {
        question: 'Is SSO really free in Vikunja?',
        answer: 'Yes. [OpenID Connect](/docs/openid) and [LDAP](/docs/ldap) are part of the free, self-hosted version and have been for years. Vikunja Pro exists, but it does not gate authentication. The [Pro FAQ](/pro) says it in so many words: you don\'t need Pro for that.',
    },
    {
        question: 'Does Vikunja have Kanban boards like Planka?',
        answer: 'Yes. Vikunja has a Kanban view with buckets you can create and reorder, plus [List, Gantt, and Table views](/help/views) on the same data. Planka is a dedicated Kanban tool and does that one thing well. Vikunja gives you Kanban as one of four ways to look at your tasks.',
    },
    {
        question: 'Can I run Vikunja on the same server as Planka?',
        answer: 'Yes. Vikunja is a single Go binary or Docker container with SQLite by default (PostgreSQL and MySQL are supported too). It runs alongside an existing Planka install while you migrate. See the [installation guide](/docs/installing).',
    },
    {
        question: 'Will Vikunja ever move SSO to Pro?',
        answer: 'The license makes that structurally hard. Vikunja is AGPL-3 with no contributor license agreement, so I don\'t hold the rights I would need to relicense contributed code. Vikunja Pro ships in the same public repository under the same license. I wrote about why this setup keeps Vikunja open in [Vikunja stays open](/changelog/vikunja-stays-open). The same reasoning applies to feature tiering.',
    },
    {
        question: 'My Planka admin account was SSO-based and I am locked out. What now?',
        answer: 'Planka 2.2.0 deactivates SSO-only users because they no longer have a password login. Planka documents how to [create a new admin user](https://docs.planka.cloud/docs/configuration/admin-user) via environment variables, so do that first to regain access and export your data. In Vikunja, OIDC users are regular users: they can be admins, they can be added to teams, and switching auth methods does not deactivate anyone.',
    },
]

export const meta = {
	title: 'Vikunja vs Planka: Self-Hosted Kanban With SSO That Stays Free',
	description: 'Looking for a Planka alternative after SSO moved to Pro? Vikunja is an open-source, self-hosted task manager with Kanban, Gantt, List, and Table views. OIDC and LDAP are in the free version and stay there.',
}
---
<Layout {...meta}>
    <Fragment slot="head">
        <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
            "@context": "https://schema.org",
            "@type": "WebPage",
            "name": "Vikunja vs Planka",
            "description": "Side-by-side comparison of Vikunja and Planka for self-hosted Kanban and project management.",
        })}></script>
    </Fragment>
    <main class="max-w-(--breakpoint-xl) mx-auto px-4 md:px-0" id="main-content">
        <div class="pt-32 pb-8 px-4 text-center">
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-display">
                Vikunja vs Planka
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-4 text-xl text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-balance">
                Self-hosted Kanban with SSO that stays in the free version.
            </p>
        </div>

        <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16 text-lg text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
            <p>
                Planka is a good Kanban board. It is fast, looks clean, and a lot of homelabs and small
                teams run it. In August 2026 the project
                <a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/issues/1754" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">moved OIDC/SSO out of the Community edition</a>
                and into the paid Pro edition. Version 2.2.0 shipped without it, and users who
                only ever logged in via SSO were deactivated on upgrade.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4">
                Where to draw the paid line is Planka's call to make. I draw it somewhere else:
                a login method shouldn't decide which tier you're on, whether you have five users or five hundred.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4">
                Vikunja is an open-source, self-hosted task manager with Kanban, List, Gantt, and
                Table views. <a href="/docs/openid" class="underline">OpenID Connect</a> and
                <a href="/docs/ldap" class="underline">LDAP</a> are freely available, documented,
                and have been for years. There is a paid <a href="/pro">Pro tier</a>, but it ships in the same public
                repository under the same AGPL-3 license, and authentication isn't part of it.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4">
                There's also a <a href="/help/import-and-export/#importing-from-planka" class="underline">Planka importer</a>:
                it pulls your boards straight out of Planka's REST API. More on that below.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-20">
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-4">What changed in Planka in 2026</h2>
            <ul class="list-disc list-outside pl-6 space-y-4 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                <li>
                    <a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/releases/tag/v2.2.0" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">Planka Community 2.2.0</a>
                    (August 2026) removed OIDC/SSO. After the update, every user who signed in through SSO
                    is deactivated until an admin sets a password for them. If the only admin account
                    was SSO-based, you are locked out and have to
                    <a href="https://docs.planka.cloud/docs/configuration/admin-user" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">create a new admin user</a> first.
                </li>
                <li>
                    The same release moved account security the other way: TOTP two-factor
                    authentication, auto-logout on inactivity, and trusted devices used to be Pro and are
                    now in Community.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Planka's <a href="https://planka.app/faq/technical" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">technical FAQ</a>
                    now says it plainly: "The Community edition has no SSO." A maintainer confirmed the
                    same to users asking about it in
                    <a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/issues/1791" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">#1791</a> and
                    <a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/issues/1807" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">#1807</a>.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Community is still getting features.
                    <a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/releases/tag/v2.3.0" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">Version 2.3.0</a>
                    (November 2026) added saved board filters, comment replies, <code>@mentions</code> in
                    card descriptions, project- and account-scoped webhooks, and a batch of security
                    hardening. 2.3.1 followed a day later with a crash fix.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mt-4">
                As of November 2026. Each point links to Planka's own announcement, release notes, or website.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-20">
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-4">What changes when you switch</h2>
            <div class="max-w-3xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 space-y-6">
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-xl">SSO is a login button</h3>
                    <p class="mt-2">
                        <a href="/docs/openid" class="underline">OIDC</a> and
                        <a href="/docs/ldap" class="underline">LDAP</a> work in the free, self-hosted
                        version. Point Vikunja at Authentik, Keycloak, Authelia, or your existing
                        directory and log in. Users who come in via OIDC are regular users with the
                        same permissions as anyone else.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-xl">A license that keeps it that way</h3>
                    <p class="mt-2">
                        Vikunja is AGPL-3 with no contributor license agreement. That means it's a constraint:
                        I don't hold the rights I would need to move contributed code into a closed tier.
                        Vikunja Pro exists and ships in the same public repo under the same license.
                        <a href="/changelog/vikunja-stays-open" class="underline">Longer explanation of how that works is here</a>.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-xl">Kanban plus Gantt and Table</h3>
                    <p class="mt-2">
                        Planka Community has
                        <a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/blob/master/server/api/models/Board.js" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">three board views</a>:
                        Kanban, List, and Grid. Timeline and calendar views are
                        <a href="https://planka.app/features" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">Pro only</a>.
                        Vikunja gives you <a href="/help/views" class="underline">List, Kanban, Gantt, and Table</a>
                        on the same data in the free version, and you can switch between them at any time.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-xl">Your data goes with you</h3>
                    <p class="mt-2">
                        Vikunja has a <a href="/help/import-and-export/#export" class="underline">full data export</a>
                        built in: projects, tasks, attachments, everything in one ZIP. If you ever
                        want to leave, you can. Planka currently has
                        <a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/issues/670" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">no native export</a>.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-xl">Lightweight to run</h3>
                    <p class="mt-2">
                        Vikunja is a single Go binary. It runs on SQLite by default, or PostgreSQL and
                        MySQL if you prefer, and it's happy on a Raspberry Pi alongside the rest of your homelab.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="font-display text-xl">CalDAV, mobile, and a full API</h3>
                    <p class="mt-2">
                        <a href="/help/caldav" class="underline">CalDAV support</a> puts your tasks in
                        Thunderbird, Apple Reminders, or any CalDAV client. Vikunja works as a
                        progressive web app on your phone, and the
                        <a href="/docs/api-documentation" class="underline">REST API</a> has full OpenAPI docs.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mt-20">
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-8">Side by side</h2>
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
                <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
                    <thead>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
                            <th class="py-3 px-4 font-display text-lg"></th>
                            <th class="py-3 px-4 font-display text-lg">Vikunja</th>
                            <th class="py-3 px-4 font-display text-lg">Planka</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">License</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">AGPL-3, no CLA</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance">Community: source-available <a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/blob/master/LICENSES/PLANKA%20Community%20License%20EN.md" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">PLANKA Community License</a> (fair-code, <a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/blob/master/LICENSES/PLANKA%20License%20Guide%20EN.md" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">not OSI open source</a>); Pro: commercial license; contributors sign a <a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/blob/master/CONTRIBUTOR_LICENSE_AGREEMENT.md" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">CLA</a></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">Self-hostable</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Yes</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Yes</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">SSO / OIDC</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance">Yes (<a href="/docs/openid" class="underline">OIDC</a>, <a href="/docs/ldap" class="underline">LDAP</a>)</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance">Pro only since 2.2.0 (<a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/issues/1754" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">issue #1754</a>)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">Kanban</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Yes</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Yes</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">Views</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">List, Kanban, Gantt, Table</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance">Community: Kanban, List, Grid. Pro adds timeline, calendar, and map views</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">Data export</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance">Full export (projects, tasks, attachments)</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance">Community: no native export (<a href="https://github.com/plankanban/planka/issues/670" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">issue #670</a>), REST API only. PDF and HTML export are <a href="https://planka.app/features" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">Pro only</a></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">Importers</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance">Trello, WeKan, Todoist, TickTick, Microsoft To Do, CSV</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Trello</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">Import from Planka</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance"><a href="/help/import-and-export/#importing-from-planka" class="underline">Yes, built in</a></td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">&mdash;</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">Backend</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Go (single binary)</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Node.js</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">Database</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">SQLite, PostgreSQL, or MySQL</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">PostgreSQL</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">CalDAV</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Yes</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">No</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">Mobile</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Progressive web app</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance">Web UI; full phone and tablet support is <a href="https://planka.app/features" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">Pro only</a></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-800">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">REST API</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance">All functionality, OpenAPI docs</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Yes</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium">Paid tier</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance">Pro, same public repo, same license</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 text-balance">Pro, separate edition under a commercial license (<a href="#planka-pro-pricing" class="underline">pricing below</a>)</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-20">
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-6" id="planka-pro-pricing">Pricing</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                Both Vikunja and Planka Community are free to self-host. The difference is where the
                paid line sits. Since 2.2.0, SSO is in Planka Pro, along with calendar and timeline views,
                recurring cards, board and card templates, PDF export, and full phone support
                (see Planka's <a href="https://planka.app/features" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">feature comparison</a>).
                Vikunja <a href="/pro" class="underline">Pro</a> adds features on top of the free version
                but leaves authentication where it is: OIDC and LDAP stay free.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mt-4">
                According to <a href="https://planka.app/pricing" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">Planka's pricing page</a>,
                Pro Self-Hosted costs 7.20&nbsp;&euro; per user per month billed yearly, or 7.90&nbsp;&euro;
                billed monthly, with lower per-user prices from 250 users. Pro Hosted starts at
                8.50&nbsp;&euro; per user per month billed yearly, with a minimum of five users. Above 1,000 users
                self-hosted (500 hosted), you talk to their Enterprise team. Prices are net of VAT, and
                Planka sells Pro to organisations only, not to private individuals.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mt-4">
                Two things to know before you try Planka Pro on an existing Community install, both from
                Planka's <a href="https://planka.app/trial" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">trial page</a>. The upgrade is one-way:
                it changes the database so Community will no longer start on it, and your pre-upgrade
                backup is the only way back. And if the 30-day trial ends without a purchase, the instance
                is locked: you can sign in and enter a key, but boards and cards are no longer shown.
                Planka recommends testing on a copy first.
            </p>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mt-4">
                If you'd rather not manage a server, <a href="/pricing" class="underline">Vikunja Cloud</a>
                starts at 4&nbsp;&euro;/month for personal use and 5&nbsp;&euro;/user/month for teams,
                hosted on EU infrastructure.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 mt-4">
                Planka prices and feature gating as of November 2026. See <a href="/pricing" class="underline">Vikunja pricing</a>
                and <a href="/pro" class="underline">Vikunja Pro</a> for details on the Vikunja side.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-20">
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-6">How to switch</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                Vikunja's Planka importer connects to your running Planka instance, so you don't need
                an export file (Planka doesn't have one anyway):
            </p>
            <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mt-4">
                <li>
                    If your admin was SSO-only and you're locked out after 2.2.0,
                    <a href="https://docs.planka.cloud/docs/configuration/admin-user" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="underline">create a new admin user</a>
                    first so you can reach your data
                </li>
                <li>
                    <a href="/docs/installing" class="underline">Set up Vikunja</a> (Docker, binary, or
                    <a href={vikunjaCloudSignupLink('compare-planka-switch')} class="underline">start a free Cloud trial</a>)
                </li>
                <li>In Vikunja, open the import page and pick Planka</li>
                <li>Enter your Planka URL and an API key, which a Planka admin has to create for you. Username and password also work, but only for local accounts without two-factor authentication; accounts that used SSO need an API key. Credentials are used for the import only and not stored</li>
                <li>Vikunja brings over your projects, boards, cards, labels, due dates, comments, attachments, and cover images. Boards become projects, lists become Kanban buckets, and cards in closed or archive lists come over as done. Checklists and custom fields are added to the task description</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mt-4 text-balance">
                What doesn't come across: assignees and board members, since your team's user
                accounts don't exist in Vikunja yet. Comments keep the author's name. The importer needs
                Planka 2 or later and Vikunja 2.6.0 or later. If you are on a Planka Pro trial, run the import
                while it is active: a locked instance no longer shows boards, cards, or attachments.
                See the <a href="/help/import-and-export/#importing-from-planka" class="underline">Planka import help page</a> for details.
            </p>
        </section>

        <FAQSection faqs={faqs} />

        <div class="pb-20 flex items-center justify-center flex-col text-center">
            <h2 class="font-display text-3xl mb-4">Give it a try</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mb-8 max-w-lg mx-auto text-balance">
                Point it at your identity provider, bring one board over, and see how it feels.
            </p>
            <CloudOrSelfHosted />
            <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 max-w-lg mx-auto text-balance">
                Running it for a team? <a href="/pro" class="underline">Vikunja Pro</a> adds audit logs, an
                admin panel, and time tracking to your self-hosted instance. Need to bring it to work?
                <a href="/convince" class="underline">Here's what to show your boss</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>
